  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "Only authoritative events essential to the delivery task are included: color-object observations, claim, pickup, drop, search, and approach for objects/zones. Communication (claim/received_claim) handles arbitration. Low-level motion commands, task_*, and obstacle events are omitted as they are either handled by fixed automata or unrelated to sequencing delivery. Only events needed for one complete color-branch box task are used.",
    "transition_design": "The automaton branches on first observed color. On <color>_object_visible, it transitions to a claim attempt for that color; claim_<color> commits the branch, otherwise received_claim_<color> or <color>_object_not_visible revert to unclaimed search. Once claimed, <color>_object_approach states use approach_object self-loops; <color>_object_not_visible returns to object search, <color>_object_visible returns to approach, and <color>_object_reached enables pickup. The flow then continues with search_zone self-loops (zone search), <color>_zone_visible to approach, and finally <color>_zone_reached enables drop_object in the finished state. All possible observation contingencies to return paths (e.g., object not visible during approach, or direct reach) are included for each color. All controllable commands only appear in protocol state-changing transitions or self-loops as required.",
